{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.YLambdaRecipeFromPartition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.YLambdaRecipeFromPartition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_recipe_n2_partition_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_recipe_n2_partition_2","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L350-L404","doc":"**Worked example, `λ = (2)` at `n = 2`**, convention D.\n\nWith `X = q⁴` the recipe reduces through the two `n = 2` partitions\n`{(2), (1,1)}` (both of dimension 1) to\n\n    y_{(2)} = (q² − q + 1)(q² + q + 1) / (q² + 1)²,\n\nwhose numerator is `Φ₆(q)·Φ₃(q) = q⁴ + q² + 1` — the cyclotomic factorisation\nof step 5, now visible over ℚ(q) rather than ℚ(√q).\n\nThe convention-C statement of this example was\n`(q·v + q + 1)/((q + 1)(q² + 1))` with `v = √q`, and it needed five\nhypotheses (`hq4`, `hp1`, `hX`, `hX1` and the derived `hXm`) purely to keep\nthe `X` denominator and the `1 − X` cancellation alive.  Under D, `X = q⁴` is\na polynomial, so those all disappear: only the two genuine hook denominators\n`1 − q²` and `1 − q⁴` remain, and `q + 1 ≠ 0` is no longer needed at all.\n\n`Z_2 = (1 + q²)²` here is the `n = 2` case of the closed form\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dim_schurPrincipal` proves at every integer level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_cyclotomic_via_recipe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_cyclotomic_via_recipe","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L343-L346","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_cyclotomic_via_recipe_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_cyclotomic_via_recipe_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L336-L341","doc":"**External axiom (Wenzl 1988):** cyclotomic factorisation of the\ny_λ recipe denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YLambdaRecipeCyclotomicFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YLambdaRecipeCyclotomicFactor","kind":"opaque","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L331-L334","doc":"**Cyclotomic factorisation**: the recipe output factors as\nP_λ(v) / D_n(v) where D_n is a pure product of cyclotomic\npolynomials Φ_d(v). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_via_recipe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_via_recipe","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L319-L329","doc":"**Plancherel completeness**: Σ_λ⊢n d_λ · y_λ(q) = 1 for every n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_via_recipe_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plancherel_via_recipe_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L308-L317","doc":"**External axiom (Wenzl 1988):** Plancherel completeness\n`Σ_λ⊢n d_λ · y_λ(q) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_recipe_correct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_recipe_correct","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L301-L306","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_recipe_correct_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_recipe_correct_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L293-L299","doc":"**External axiom (Wenzl 1988):** y_λ recipe matches the canonical\nJones-Markov coefficient via Macdonald hook telescope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovTagged_convention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovTagged_convention","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L287-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovTagged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovTagged","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L281-L285","doc":"The Wenzl–Schur-tagged y_λ wrapper. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaRecipeConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaRecipeConvention","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L277-L279","doc":"The Markov-trace convention this recipe implements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.JonesMarkovCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.JonesMarkovCoefficient","kind":"opaque","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L253-L275","doc":"**Recipe correctness**: the algorithm `yLambdaRecipe` produces the\nJones-Markov central coefficient y_λ for the symmetric Hecke\nconvention σ² = (q - q⁻¹)σ + 1 with parameter z = 1/(v + v⁻¹).\n\nThe output is **Wenzl–Schur-canonical**: `JonesMarkovCoefficient`\nis the y_λ on the Wenzl-Schur side of the convention split (see\n`MarkovTraceConvention`). Plancherel-derived y_λ values do not\nsatisfy this theorem and are not interchangeable.\n\nEquivalent to prop:y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge restated\nalgorithmically.\n\nAbstract external constant (`axiom`, not `opaque`): the canonical\nJones–Markov coefficient is an external datum ([wenzl1988]); `opaque\n… : R` over generic `Field R` fails v4.24 code-gen (see\n`partitionFunctionZ`), so it is declared as an `axiom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient.convention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient.convention","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L249-L249","doc":"The Markov-trace convention this value follows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient.value","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L247-L247","doc":"The y_λ value at the substrate parameter (in the ground ring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient.mk","kind":"ctor","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L245-L245","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceCoefficient","kind":"structure","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L240-L249","doc":"A Markov-trace y_λ value paired with the convention it\nimplements. Wrapping a raw `value` in this structure lets\ndownstream theorems pattern-match on the `convention` field\nrather than relying on prose annotations or external audit\ndocs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprMarkovTraceConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprMarkovTraceConvention","kind":"instance","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L238-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprMarkovTraceConvention.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprMarkovTraceConvention.repr","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L238-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqMarkovTraceConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqMarkovTraceConvention","kind":"instance","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L238-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceConvention.wenzlSchur","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceConvention.wenzlSchur","kind":"ctor","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L237-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceConvention.plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceConvention.plancherel","kind":"ctor","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L236-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceConvention","kind":"inductive","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L235-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaRecipe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaRecipe","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L211-L215","doc":"The recipe: `y_λ(q) = s_{λ, r}(Q) / Z_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.partitionFunctionZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.partitionFunctionZ","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L204-L209","doc":"Partition-function denominator `Z_n = Σ_µ d_µ · s_µ` — a **concrete**\nsum over the shared `partitionsOf n` with `d_µ = hookDim µ`,\n`s_µ = schurPrincipal µ` (de-axiomatised; computable). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.schurPrincipal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.schurPrincipal","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L176-L195","doc":"The Schur principal-specialisation factor for partition λ at\nlevel r, with `Q = q²` and `X = Q^r`:\n\n  s_{λ, r}(Q) = Q^{n(λ)} · ∏_{(i,j) ∈ λ} (1 - X·Q^{c(i,j)}) / (1 - Q^{h(i,j)})\n\nConcrete cell-product: outer fold over rows `(row-length, row-index)`\n(the `hookDim` iteration pattern), inner fold over columns `j`.  The\ncontent `c(i,j) : ℤ` gives an integer power `Q ^ (c : ℤ)` (zpow); the\nhook `h(i,j) : ℕ` gives a natural power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.universalX_eq_lattice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.universalX_eq_lattice","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L156-L172","doc":"**`X` is on the Wenzl lattice at level 2.**  `X = z_W/(1 − Q + z_W)`\nwith `Q = q²` — the relation that pins the level — evaluates to `q⁴`,\ni.e. `Q²`, so the convention-D recipe sits at the integer level `r = 2`.\n\nThis is the lemma the old convention-C form could not state: there the\nsame inversion gives `z_W = q^{3/2}/(q+1)` and an effective level of\nabout `2.5995` at the substrate anchor, which is not an integer and so\nnot on the lattice at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.universalX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.universalX","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L152-L154","doc":"**Universal X**, convention D: `X = Q^r` at `Q = q²`, `r = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovZW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovZW","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L146-L150","doc":"The **Wenzl-normalised** parameter `z_W = q · z_D`.  The factor `q` is\nthe Hecke-normalisation shift between `g² = (Q−1)g + Q` and\n`σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1`, under which `σ = g/q` and `Q = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovZ","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L142-L144","doc":"**Convention-D Markov parameter** `z_D = q³/(q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hookDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hookDim","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L127-L134","doc":"Hook-length dimension formula: f^λ = n! / ∏ h(i, j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nPartition","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L122-L125","doc":"n(λ) := Σ (i-1) λ_i  -- the standard partition statistic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellHook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellHook","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L109-L120","doc":"Hook length h(i, j) for the cell at row i, column j of partition λ\n(rows and columns 0-indexed):\narm + leg + 1 where\n  arm(i, j) := λ_i - (j + 1)  (cells strictly right of (i, j) in row i)\n  leg(i, j) := |{r > i : λ_r > j}|  (cells below in column j) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellContent","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean#L106-L107","doc":"Content c(i, j) := j - i for the cell at row i, column j (1-indexed). ","signatureChunk":0}]}